Subject: An API client's own Bot Chat stays an API conversation

Under session authority any text turn into the canonical "Bot Chat" (POST /v1/runs, /api/sessions/{id}/chat)
went to the authority FIFO (admit_peer_turn) and a Bot Chat an API client had made was moved aside as
"Bot Chat (API <id>)" on the first such turn, a new empty local Bot Chat taking its title. A client that makes
and runs its Bot Chat through the API (BipAgents: each agent's main conversation) lost its history and got a run
stream with only run.completed: no text deltas, no tool events, no model.usage, no clarify.

A Bot Chat made by a plain POST /api/sessions (source api_server, no local chat in its lineage) is now the
client's: create_peer_bot_chat leaves such a create to the ordinary handler (a peer's create names its source,
bot_peer_dm, and still mints the local chat), displaceable_bot_chat never moves it aside, and admit_peer_turn
leaves its turns to the API doors, which run them as API turns as before session authority. Local doors
(bot_relay, cron bot-chat) into it are refused instead of moving it. Every other Bot Chat is unchanged.

BipAgents patch, documented in hermes/patches/README.md of the BipAgents repository.

Bip-Patch: 0021-api-bot-chat-stays-api
